# SEO & AEO

Goal: each published app is the **citable source** for “what is {app}, who makes it, iOS/Android, free/paid.”

## Google (people-first)

- Unique `hero.seoTitle` (≤58) and `hero.metaDescription` (≤155) via `buildProductPageMetadata`
- H1 = product name; first paragraph answers what the app does
- One primary intent per URL; no keyword stuffing or hidden text
- JSON-LD must match **visible** copy (`FAQPage` / `HowTo` only if those sections exist)
- Never invent `AggregateRating` / review counts — `lib/appStoreRatings.ts` only when live
- Image `alt` describes the screen, not “screenshot 1”
- Canonical + hreflang on every indexable route

## AI engines (citation-ready)

Keep these four in lockstep after every copy change:

| Surface | File |
|---------|------|
| HTML + JSON-LD | `layout.tsx` + page sections |
| Crawler Q&A | `public/{slug}/faq.md` — question headings, first sentence = quotable fact, absolute `https://zukiapps.com/...` URLs |
| Machine index | `public/llms.txt` expanded bullet (stores, package IDs, faq.md) |
| Catalog JSON | `public/site-facts.json` (static host has no `/api/*`) |
| Short stub | `public/ai.txt` if adding a **new** app |

Entity name is always **Zuki Apps**. Include platforms, Android package, iOS id, price model, and what the app does **not** do. No puffery (“best”, “revolutionary”).

`app/robots.ts` must keep GPTBot, ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, Google-Extended **allowed**.

## Verify

```bash
npm run build
```

Spot-check: unique titles, store URLs 200, package IDs match Play / App Store Connect.

Playbook: `.cursor/skills/product-page-enrichment/SKILL.md`
